+.SH RIPPLE NOTES
+This port uses binary64 software arithmetic and a C locale with an octet
+regular-expression alphabet. Input characters above 255 are rejected.
+Dynamic records/format buffers are limited to 16000 native characters;
+other storage is limited by the process heap. The default record allocation
+is 1024 characters and grows as required. Decimal floating output rounds
+the exact binary64 value, with precision fields up to 30.
+.PP
+Integer printf conversions use signed/unsigned 32-bit values. Multibyte
+locale conversion and hexadecimal floating output are not supplied. Files,
+redirections, command pipes, getline, system, arrays and functions run
+through the guest's own libc and kernel.
